const pages=[
 ['Settings and workspace modes','Settings in the top bar contains Scaffold and the Properties panel preference. Scaffold on gives a guided workspace: Shapes opens a chooser, Object options holds the selected artwork’s actions, and Canvas options, Sequencer options and Keyframe options contain their controls. Scaffold off keeps detailed controls visible in compact rows and Shapes opens an inline strip. Both modes retain every tool, animation feature, selection outline and editing handle. Preferences are remembered on this device. Settings → Composition settings changes size, duration, frame rate and background; Project also has that command.'],
 ['Open or collapse Properties','Properties beside the canvas toggles the inspector on any screen. The ‹ button in its heading collapses it. Keep it collapsed for more canvas room, or open it for exact transform, colour, text, mesh and reference settings. All Properties in Object options opens the same panel. Settings can also keep it open.'],
 ['Sequencer blocks and playback','Playback controls sit above the sequencer. Tap the ruler to set time; in Select/move blocks mode, tap a block to select it and drag to move it. Empty lanes pan. Scrub time mode makes lane drags scrub instead. Pinch with two fingers to zoom the sequencer around the midpoint; + and − give the same zoom. Select a block, put the playhead inside it and choose Split. Start/End plus Trim shorten it. Copy/Paste repeats the selected block at the playhead. Audio blocks keep their source sound when split or trimmed.'],
 ['Block parameter graphs','Double-tap an animation block, or select it and tap Edit tracks. Each animated parameter gets a sublane on the same time scale. Choose X, Y, rotation, opacity, path, mesh or another parameter to edit its keys and outgoing tween. Changes apply only during that block. Canvas edits at a time inside the block key its own enabled tracks. Key at block start and Key at last frame set the endpoints.'],
 ['Loop, tempo and more time','Sequence / + time sets a playback loop with start and length. Use Seconds, Frames, or optional Bars. Tempo and beats per bar define a bar; they do not stretch existing animation. Turn Loop on to preview only that range. Whole composition resets the range. + Add seconds extends time. Full-sequence copy/paste repeats selected layers or all animation; audio is copied separately as blocks.'],
 ['Movement reference','Choose Walk, Run, Sprint, Hop or Slide and rotate the basic jointed puppet by dragging or entering degrees. The live pose label marks contact, down, passing and up; running adds flight. Heel-to-toe support, weight shift, curved foot recovery, opposing arms and delayed hands/head make the poses easier to trace. Hop loads before takeoff and absorbs the landing; Slide stays grounded. In-place support feet move steadily backward against a virtual moving floor. Set the cycle length and insertion time, then Bake reference layer. Transparent PNG frames become a locked layer below artwork. Properties controls opacity and export inclusion; references are excluded from export by default. Baking is limited to 10 seconds and 600 frames.'],
 ['Onion skins and exact frames','Onion skin shows previous and next artwork frames for tracing motion. Choose 1, 2 or 3 frames and opacity. Ghosts disappear during playback and stay out of exports. Previous/Next frame steps exactly one project frame. Snap frames controls scrubbing; block and key edits always snap to frames. The playback row shows the current frame and save/export status.'],
 ['Bevel and texture','With Scaffold on, open Object options for these actions; with Scaffold off, use the visible editing row. In Direct mode, select a path point and change its bevel radius or round/bevel style. Image texture imports an image clipped inside a closed shape: Cover crops to fill, Fit shows the whole image, and Stretch or Tile offer other placement. Scale and X/Y offset adjust the image. Apply keeps one undo step; Cancel restores the original.'],
 ['Start drawing','Open Shapes and choose Rectangle, Ellipse, Triangle, Polygon, Star or Line. Drag on the canvas: the shape starts under your finger. A double tap places a standard-sized shape with its top-left corner at your finger. A single empty-canvas tap deselects. New artwork uses your last colour. Pencil follows your strokes. Path lets you tap anchors and drag to curve; finish with “Finish path”.'],
 ['Select and edit','Select taps the frontmost shape at your pointer. Use the layer list for artwork behind it, or Direct to reach a child inside a group. Drag selected artwork after the small movement threshold. A touch drag on empty canvas pans; to select several shapes, hold empty canvas for 350 ms until “Marquee ready”, then drag a box. Moving before the hold finishes pans instead. Mouse/pen can drag empty canvas directly to select a set. Direct exposes square path points; tap one to reveal its round curve handles. Zoom in for dense points or use ‹ Point / Point ›. Edit points converts rectangles and ellipses to paths. Text stays editable in Properties.'],
 ['Precise movement','Objects follow your finger at the same distance. Precision reduces the movement to 35% for fine adjustments. Snap is optional and starts off. Corner and edge handles resize; the handle above rotates. Constrain keeps proportions; Resize from center uses the centre. Two fingers pan and zoom the canvas.'],
 ['Group layers','Turn on Multi-select in Canvas options or the visible canvas controls, then tap shapes or layer names. Choose Group in Object options, or the visible selection controls with Scaffold off. Ungroup releases the shapes; animated or partially transparent groups must have their group tracks removed and opacity restored first. Direct edits a child inside a group; Select contents selects its children. Locked layers cannot be edited.'],
 ['Combine shapes and paths','Turn on Multi-select and choose at least two closed shapes in the same group. Unite joins their filled areas. Subtract front cuts the shapes in front out of the back shape. Keep overlap keeps only their shared area. Exclude overlap cuts away their shared area. Compound path keeps all outlines in one editable shape, with overlaps becoming holes. Combining creates editable points from the current frame and replaces the originals; Undo restores them. Join paths connects the nearest ends of two open paths.'],
 ['Animate in five steps','1. Draw or select a shape.\n2. Put the playhead at 0 seconds and press Add keyframe. This enables movement, rotation, scale and opacity tracks. In Direct mode it also enables path-point animation.\n3. Tap or drag the timeline ruler to a later time, such as 2 seconds.\n4. Move, resize or rotate the shape. Its enabled properties get new keyframes at that time. In Direct mode you can drag points to create shape keys.\n5. Return to the beginning and press Play. Adjust the Tween menu to choose smooth easing, linear motion or a hold.'],
 ['Animate colour or points','In Properties, tap the ◇ beside Fill or Stroke to enable colour animation, then go to a later time and change its colour. For a path, use Animate points or Add keyframe in Direct mode, then edit the same points later. Keep the same number of points and curve handles for a smooth shape tween. Adding/deleting points changes topology. For a mesh, choose Animate mesh at the start, then move the playhead and change point colours or positions. These edits create keys on the Mesh shading track. Subdivision updates all mesh keys together so they can still tween. Explicit mesh keys retain their own geometry when path points animate; use Fit to shape at a key if needed.'],
 ['Edit individual track keys','Each track has its own diamond button to add a key at the playhead. Tap a track’s key to select it and go to its time. Edit key changes only that key’s time, value and tween to the next key. Path shape keys are edited on the canvas. Copy, Paste and Delete keys affect the selected keys.'],
 ['Layer shadows','Select a shape and choose Layer in the canvas dock, or ⋯ beside its layer name. Enable drop shadow, adjust horizontal/vertical offsets, blur, opacity and colour. Sliders and exact numbers preview changes immediately. Apply keeps them in one undo step; Cancel restores the original. Animate shadow enables separate tracks. Shadows are included in transparent PNG frames, SVG and video.'],
 ['Graph editor','Choose Graph for the selected layer. Select a track. Drag numeric keys horizontally for time and vertically for value, or type exact values. Drag round tween handles to create a custom Bézier curve for the selected key’s outgoing segment. Path, mesh and colour tracks show tween progress; edit their artwork on the canvas. Frames measurement applies to graph axes and key-time fields. On small screens, swipe the empty graph horizontally; handles remain finger-sized.'],
 ['Repeat a sequence and add time','Sequence / + time copies the full composition duration of selected layers or all animated layers, then repeats those tracks on the same objects. Append at end extends the duration automatically. At playhead replaces overlapping keys; the preview shows the number before pasting. Audio is not copied. + Add seconds extends time without stretching artwork or audio. Seconds / Frames switches timeline and graph measurement; frames are numbered from zero.'],
 ['Line styles and profiles','Select a line and use the visible Width, Style and Profile controls. Styles are solid, dashed or dotted; profiles can taper either end, both ends, or make a brush bulge. Properties has end-cap and corner controls. Stroke width has its own animation track.'],
 ['Shade with a mesh','Select an individual closed, filled shape and choose Mesh. With Scaffold on, its actions are in Object options. Set mesh bounds asks for two taps: one side/corner inside the fill, then the opposite side/corner. Add mesh point lets you tap inside that shading area and away from holes; an interior tap adds the corresponding grid row/column while retaining existing points and colours. Tap a point to select it, drag to move it, or hold for 550 ms to open its colour panel. Point colour opens the same panel; movement cancels the hold. Animate mesh at the first time, then move the playhead and change colours/positions to create Mesh shading keys. Insertion/subdivision updates every mesh key together. Fit to shape restores an outline-fitting grid while keeping colours. The practical limit is 17 × 17 grid points; start small and split highly concave/disjoint artwork into separate shaded shapes when needed. This is a structured Poppy grid, not unlimited independent nodes or an Illustrator mesh import. Shading is clipped to the shape and exports to video/SVG as a PNG capped at 640 pixels on its longer edge.'],
 ['Save and export','Changes save on this device. Project → Export project file makes a portable .poppy backup to open on another device. Export video renders the animation and audio together. The resolution and supported format appear before rendering. Every launch starts with a blank canvas; Project → Open local project restores saved work.'],
];
export function showHelp(a){const d=a.dialog('Help · Draw it. Tween it.',`<div class="help-intro">Your quick guide to Poppy’s Animator</div><div class="help-pages">${pages.map(([title,body],i)=>`<details ${title==='Animate in five steps'?'open':''}><summary>${title}</summary><p>${body.replaceAll('\n','<br>')}</p></details>`).join('')}</div><div class="help-shortcuts">Transparent frames: Export → Transparent PNG frames (ZIP) renders numbered frames without the canvas background. The ZIP includes sequence.json with the frame rate. PNG sequences have no audio. Keyboard: V Select · A Direct select · M Mesh · R Rectangle · E Ellipse · B Path · Space Play · Ctrl/⌘Z Undo</div>`);d.classList.add('help-dialog');}
